        "id": 143016,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-07-17T13:17:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes! Earth is perigee/apogee (“gee” like “geo”) for closest and farthest points. The Moon is -lune, the sun is -helion, Mars is -areon, Jupiter is -jove, Saturn is -krone. Those are the ones I remember offhand. And I know there’s a super cool one for black holes, but I forgot it…</p>\n<p>The general terms are periapsis and apoapsis. There’s a bunch more terms collected in the Wikipedia article for “apsis.”</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
